# Working idea: restaurant ops software for small independent restaurants

Problem: small family restaurants (like my parents' 40-seat place in San Jose) run on thin margins with spreadsheets, paper schedules, and manual inventory. Enterprise POS tools are priced and built for chains.

Idea: a lightweight tool that handles weekly food-cost tracking, supplier price changes, and staff scheduling for owners with 1-3 locations.

First step: shadow my parents' restaurant for two weeks, map where the time goes, build a prototype for one workflow (food cost tracking), and test it with them as the first user.

Why me: CS degree, web dev and Python, and I know the operator's side from the inside.

## Week 8 update
Food-cost tracker for restaurants. Next step: review two months of real invoices with parents (Thursday). Goal: a paying or pilot restaurant customer, which unlocks acc-04 (Main Street Tech Incubator) and angel-02 later. Meridian rejected me; keep the IT support job as the cash base.

Week 9: Applied to job-11 (Solutions Engineer, Fernway). Asked parents to be a paying pilot for the food-cost tracker and to help with a friends-and-family intro (angel-06). Next: get a written pilot agreement and a short money plan before applying to angel-06 and acc-04 (needs one pilot customer).

## Week 14 update
- Now a full-time Solutions Engineer at Fernway Payments ($2,200/week). Cash covers living costs with room to save.
- Friends-and-family round declined; will reapply once there are paying users beyond family.
- Plan: keep the food-cost tracker running on the parents' restaurant data, aim for a second paying restaurant, and build toward a prototype that can meet accelerator and angel requirements later (fall, after the job settles).
- Savings floor: keep at least 12 weeks of expenses in cash before any startup spending.

## Week 15
Fernway job is stable. Tracker tests pass (test_cost, test_latest_price_wins). Next: ask parents for their weekly seafood and produce numbers to test the tracker on real invoices, then aim for a second restaurant pilot. Savings floor still 12 weeks of expenses before startup spending.

